  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Rajesh Gupta vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh on 8 January, 2020 Author: Rajendra Kumar Srivastava Bench: Rajendra Kumar Srivastava 1 Mcrc-34877-2019 The High Court Of Madhya Pradesh Mcrc-34877-2019 (Rajesh Gupta Vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh And Others) 4 Jabalpur, Dated : 08-01-2020 Shri Sankalp Kochar, Advocate for the petitioner. Shri Sharad Singh Baghel, P.L. for the respondent-State.",
    "facts": "Learned counsel for the petitioner submits that on 27.07.2019, complainant alongwith few other officers visited the factory of the applicant in the garb of ensuring compliance the provisions of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006. The said team of officers alongwith the respondent no.2/complainant took the samples of certain raw materials as well as processed material from the factory and found as Sub-standard under the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 and registered an FIR No. 197/2019 at P.S.-Industrial Area, Satlapur, Distt.-Raisen under Section 272, 273 & 420 of IPC. He submits that the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 is special enactment, which specifically deals with the offence of sub-standard product, thus, the penal provision of IPC do not apply in this matter. complainant- respondent no.2 has not followed the procedure of law, as provided under Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006. On these grounds, he prays for staying the further proceedings of the aforesaid First Information Report.",
